WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.359 --> 00:00:02.949
Hello World, Shawn Grooms here with Free Code
Camp.

00:00:02.949 --> 00:00:07.110
And in this video I will be giving you three
tips on how to learn Discrete Mathematics.

00:00:07.110 --> 00:00:09.870
The first tip is to stay calm.

00:00:09.870 --> 00:00:13.809
People often hear the word Mathematics and
panic.

00:00:13.809 --> 00:00:15.929
When you panic, you stop listening.

00:00:15.929 --> 00:00:18.800
If you stop listening, you can't learn the
material.

00:00:18.800 --> 00:00:23.480
If you simply stay calm, then you'll be able
to learn the material better.

00:00:23.480 --> 00:00:27.160
You aren't being graded on the subject so
there's no need to panic.

00:00:27.160 --> 00:00:30.000
The second is to rewind.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:32.890
You can rewind the videos at any time.

00:00:32.890 --> 00:00:36.550
When I learned Discrete Mathematics I didn't
have this opportunity.

00:00:36.550 --> 00:00:41.120
In theory you should be able to learn the
material much faster than I was ever able

00:00:41.120 --> 00:00:42.120
to.

00:00:42.120 --> 00:00:46.190
I strongly encourage rewinding the video.

00:00:46.190 --> 00:00:47.790
Finally, explain.

00:00:47.790 --> 00:00:53.440
Once you think you understand the material
of the videos you can try to explain the material

00:00:53.440 --> 00:00:56.170
out loud either to yourself or to a friend.

00:00:56.170 --> 00:01:00.540
If no one is around, or you feel weird talking
to yourself then you can try and explain it

00:01:00.540 --> 00:01:02.800
to a rubber ducky.

00:01:02.800 --> 00:01:08.830
There's a concept in Programming called Rubber
Ducky debugging, which is where programmers

00:01:08.830 --> 00:01:14.420
go through their code, line by line, trying
to identify bugs in their code by explaining

00:01:14.420 --> 00:01:16.000
it to a rubber ducky.

00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:21.670
So similarly, if you go through the material
of the videos, subject by subject, you will

00:01:21.670 --> 00:01:26.810
soon be able to identify any gaps in your
understanding of the material.

